1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,000
In this video, we will learn how to reverse-activate and shrink the filter to complete a multi-layered clothing dress.

2
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:12,000
First, we will transfer the material to the work area.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:15,000
In this case, I will add a little bit of T-shirt to show you later.

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:17,000
We create a belt plate and reverse-activate them.

5
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:20,000
After the plate is reversed, it will not participate in the simulation and there will be no conflict.

6
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:25,000
Select a set of plates and modify the tail shrink to make the clothes become tight.

7
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:31,000
Combine the belt plates together, then activate them and start the simulation.

8
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:35,000
Now the belt is correctly worn on the outside of the clothes.

9
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Harden the belt to make it more stable and wrap it around the outside.

10
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:41,000
Then increase the tail shrink rate of the chain group to 100.

11
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:44,000
Now that the layer is stable, we will add another coat.

12
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:46,000
After the inner layer is worn, we can freeze all the inner layers.

13
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:50,000
Let them have a conflict with other layers while maintaining their shape.

14
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:54,000
Now we add a coat, start the simulation and adjust the shape of the clothes.

